  "originalQuery": "Your company is deploying a Bare Metal Solution for Oracle in Region A and requires the machine to access a Cloud SQL database in Region B. You have established a Dedicated Interconnect between your on-premises network and Region A. What networking configuration should you implement to allow the Bare Metal Solution machine to securely connect to the Cloud SQL database in Region B?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Add a static route to the Bare Metal Solution routing table for Region B.<br/>B. Create a Cloud VPN tunnel between the Bare Metal Solution in Region A and Region B.<br/>C. Enable global dynamic routing for your VPC network.<br/>D. Configure a private Google access gateway for the VPC in Region A.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
